# ThreadSanitizer suppressions.
#
# core:mem/virtual reserves and releases memory with raw `mmap`/`munmap`
# syscalls (core/mem/virtual/virtual_linux.odin), which ThreadSanitizer cannot
# intercept. Address reuse across threads is therefore reported as a data race
# in the allocator itself. Suppress those frames; races elsewhere still fail.
race:mem_virtual::*
